What are Remanufactured Gas Turbines?
Remanufactured gas turbines represent a high-value engineering process where decommissioned or used turbines undergo comprehensive refurbishment to restore original performance specifications or better. Unlike basic repairs, this process involves complete disassembly, advanced diagnostics, replacement of worn components with upgraded materials, and precision reassembly - typically achieving 80-90% of new unit performance at 30-50% lower capital cost.
These systems play a critical role in power generation, oil & gas, and industrial applications where operators must balance reliability requirements with capital expenditure constraints. The remanufacturing process follows strict OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer) standards while incorporating technological upgrades that often improve upon the turbine's original efficiency and emissions profile.
